{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"update-stage26.json\", \"summary\": \"Source-only item for the remaining budget: the log-store interface duties and the two documented contracts that decide what log entries mean (valid:true).\\n\\nRecorded behaviours and an explained investigation, no defect claim:\\n`LogStore` promises `FirstIndex`/`LastIndex` returning 0 when there are no entries, requires `GetLog`/`StoreLog`/`DeleteRange` (inclusive), and explicitly permits `StoreLogs` to leave a gap between previous logs and the stored batch. The library depends on that freedom: the gap is the signal that logs before a restored snapshot are discontinuous, and stores that cannot tolerate gaps must opt in through `MonotonicLogStore.IsMonotonic`, after which Raft removes all previous logs instead of relying on the gap (log.go:110-143). The captured in-memory store inserts by index and does not implement the opt-in (inmem_store.go:66-78), so it takes the gap branch — consistent with the fork already seen in the install path.\\n\\nThe two contracts worth keeping: `LogBarrier` exists so preceding operations reach the FSM and resolves only when the FSM manager acknowledges it (log.go:33-38), which is stronger than a committed no-op and lines up with the apply-path ordering established earlier in this run; and a log entry's `AppendedAt` is explicitly operational only — not used for coordination or replication, followers may see a future timestamp from clock skew, and the leader is not required to persist before delivering (log.go:96-107) — a negative that stops age metrics from being read as ordering or freshness. The `oldestLog` helper additionally tolerates truncation racing with its read by retrying until the first index is stable or a hard error appears (log.go:145-175).\\n\\nLimitations are stated: source-only, no custom store written and no gap-dependent resynchronisation executed, third-party stores outside this snapshot not inspected, and the call-site survey limited to the paths read in this run. The only consumer/producer mismatch identified belongs to a store implementation that needs monotonicity without declaring it, which is outside the captured snapshot.\"}"}}
